    "# Quiz: The Data Science Lifecycle: Communication\n",
    "\n",
    "> **On Alps:** These are the questions of this lesson's pre-lecture and post-lecture quizzes, from the course's quiz app, with the answers the quiz app accepts."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Pre-lecture quiz"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "metadata": {
    "format": "application/vnd.pretext+xml"
   },
   "source": [
    "<exercise label=\"dsb-quiz-16-pre-1\">\n",
    "  <statement>\n",
    "    <p>When communicating data to an audience, it is a best practice to focus solely on the numbers and not the story.</p>\n",
    "  </statement>\n",
    "  <choices randomize=\"no\">\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>True</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. Your aim is to tell a story informed by your data. People remember a story more than a number.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice correct=\"yes\">\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>False</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Correct. Tell a story informed by your data. An audience remembers a story better than a number.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "  </choices>\n",
    "</exercise>"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "metadata": {
    "format": "application/vnd.pretext+xml"
   },
   "source": [
    "<exercise label=\"dsb-quiz-16-pre-2\">\n",
    "  <statement>\n",
    "    <p>Which is an example of Two-Way Communication?</p>\n",
    "  </statement>\n",
    "  <choices randomize=\"no\">\n",
    "    <choice correct=\"yes\">\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>When a presenter presents to an audience and leaves the floor open for questions &amp; feedback.</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Correct. When the audience can ask questions and give feedback, both sides send and receive information.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>When a leader puts out a TV or Radio message to their constituents.</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. A TV or radio message gets no response, so it is one-way communication.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>When a brand advertises to potential customers.</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. Ads send information without asking for a response, like a TV commercial. That is one-way.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "  </choices>\n",
    "</exercise>"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "metadata": {
    "format": "application/vnd.pretext+xml"
   },
   "source": [
    "<exercise label=\"dsb-quiz-16-pre-3\">\n",
    "  <statement>\n",
    "    <p>When an individual is presenting to an audience, and the audience is not providing any feedback, who is acting as the information receiver?</p>\n",
    "  </statement>\n",
    "  <choices randomize=\"no\">\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>The presenter</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. The presenter is the sender. The audience is the receiver.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice correct=\"yes\">\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>The audience</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Correct. The audience receives the information, even when it gives no feedback.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>Specific members of the audience</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. The whole audience is the receiver, not just some of its members.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "  </choices>\n",
    "</exercise>"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Post-lecture quiz"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "metadata": {
    "format": "application/vnd.pretext+xml"
   },
   "source": [
    "<exercise label=\"dsb-quiz-16-post-1\">\n",
    "  <statement>\n",
    "    <p>When communicating data, colors can be used to evoke emotion from the audience.</p>\n",
    "  </statement>\n",
    "  <choices randomize=\"no\">\n",
    "    <choice correct=\"yes\">\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>True</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Correct. Different colors evoke different emotions, like blue for peace and trust.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>False</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. Different colors evoke different emotions, like yellow for optimism and happiness.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "  </choices>\n",
    "</exercise>"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "metadata": {
    "format": "application/vnd.pretext+xml"
   },
   "source": [
    "<exercise label=\"dsb-quiz-16-post-2\">\n",
    "  <statement>\n",
    "    <p>Of the options below, which is the most meaningful explanation of a company's yearly progress?</p>\n",
    "  </statement>\n",
    "  <choices randomize=\"no\">\n",
    "    <choice correct=\"yes\">\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>We had an excellent year! Our users grew by 30%, our revenue increased by 21%, and we've added 100 new team members.</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Correct. Exact numbers make the message clear, so everyone gets the same idea of the results.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>We had a great year! Our users grew tremendously, our revenue increased by a lot, and we even added several new team members across all divisions.</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. Words like \"tremendously\" and \"a lot\" are vague. Each listener may picture something different.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>Our progress year was simply phenomenal. I can't overstate how much of an increase we've had with growing our users, our revenue, or our team.</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. This gives no numbers. Vague words leave each listener with a different idea of the results.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "  </choices>\n",
    "</exercise>"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "metadata": {
    "format": "application/vnd.pretext+xml"
   },
   "source": [
    "<exercise label=\"dsb-quiz-16-post-3\">\n",
    "  <statement>\n",
    "    <p>When communicating data to an Executive Audience, which would be an acceptable strategy to take?</p>\n",
    "  </statement>\n",
    "  <choices randomize=\"no\">\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>Go in depth with the small details and spend less time on the significance of the data.</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. Executives only have time to grasp the significance and conclusions, not small details.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice correct=\"yes\">\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>Focus primarily on the significance of the data and the recommended next steps based on the data.</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Correct. Executives only have time to grasp the significance and conclusions of the data.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>Explain the entire context and try to brainstorm potential solutions with the executives.</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. Executives have little time. Give them the significance and conclusions, not the full context.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "  </choices>\n",
    "</exercise>"
   ]
  }
 ],
